menu "uDisplay"

    config UDISPLAY_ENABLE_NIMBLE
        bool "NimBLE BLE transport backend"
        depends on BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Build libudisplay's built-in BLE transport (udisplay_nimble.h):
            the uDisplay GATT service, advertising, connection lifecycle and
            outbound indication queue on top of NimBLE. Firmware then only
            calls udisplay_nimble_init()/udisplay_nimble_start().

            Needs legacy advertising (BT_NIMBLE_EXT_ADV off). Firmware must
            not send indications of its own on the uDisplay connection.

            Off by default, even with NimBLE enabled: firmware that runs its
            own BLE code, or no BLE at all, gets no NimBLE dependency from
            libudisplay.

    config UDISPLAY_NIMBLE_TX_QUEUE_BYTES
        int "Outbound fragment queue size (bytes)"
        depends on UDISPLAY_ENABLE_NIMBLE
        range 1400 32768
        default 2048
        help
            Static buffer holding fragments waiting for their turn to be
            indicated (one indication is in flight at a time). Each fragment
            costs its length plus 2 bytes. It must hold the largest burst
            the library sends between two confirmations: a 1 KB message at
            the default 23-byte MTU is about 1.3 KB, hence the minimum.
            Overflow drops the link.

endmenu
